IMPORT prelude

-- Parks and Trees Act 2005 (Singapore) -- when cutting a tree or plant needs the Commissioner's approval (ss 8, 14, 18, 27), releasing
-- animals in national parks and nature reserves (s 9(3)), the maximum penalties for the main offences (ss 8-10, 14, 18, 19, 24, 26, 27,
-- 43, 44, 46), the vehicle owner's liability (s 45), the due-diligence defence to non-compliance with a notice (s 46(2)), composition
-- (s 51), appeals to the Minister (s 56), and the Government's immunity from prosecution (s 3).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PTA2005.txt. The revised edition
-- incorporates amendments up to 1 December 2021; later amendments annotated in the deposit run to Act 42 of 2022 (wef 1 November 2024)
-- and Act 23 of 2023 (wef 18 December 2023, s 59A).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 7 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to what a landowner, developer, motorist or
-- park visitor meets: the approval requirements for cutting trees, the offences and their maxima, and the routes out (exceptions,
-- defences, composition, appeal). Not encoded: appointments (ss 4-6A), designation of areas (ss 7, 13, 16) and the Schedule, the
-- content of reinstatement, enforcement and maintenance notices, planting-area dimensions and specifications (ss 22-23, 32-36),
-- public-park vesting (ss 28-29), street works (s 31), enforcement powers (ss 37-42C), cost recovery (ss 46A-48), evidence and
-- presumptions (ss 53, 54) beyond a comment, and regulations.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Parks and Trees Act 2005 -- trees, plants and offences`

DECLARE Place IS ONE OF
    `a national park`
    `a nature reserve`
    `a tree conservation area`
    `vacant land`
    `a heritage road green buffer`
    `a green margin planted under a s 27 notice`
    `an occupied private garden outside any designated area`

§§ `8, 14, 18, 27 -- cutting a tree or plant`

-- s 8(1)(a): "A person must not, except with the approval of the Commissioner granted under section 12 ... cut, collect or displace
-- any tree or plant or any part thereof" within any national park or nature reserve. s 8(4): not the Commissioner, an authorised
-- officer, a park ranger or a Board employee acting in duty, or a police officer or workman assisting them. s 8 has NO exception for
-- a tree that is an immediate threat (contrast ss 14(6), 18(4), 27(4)); s 38 lets the Commissioner act on such a tree.
-- s 14(1): must not, without approval under s 20, "cut any tree with a girth exceeding one metre" growing on a tree conservation area
-- or "any vacant land (whether within or outside a tree conservation area)". (6): "No approval ... is required where the condition
-- of the tree constitutes an immediate threat to life or property."
-- s 18(1): must not, without approval under s 20, "cut any tree or plant within a heritage road green buffer" -- no girth threshold.
-- (4): no approval where (a) "the tree or plant is determined by the Commissioner as dying or dead" or (b) immediate threat.
-- s 27(2): "A person must not, at any time, cut or damage any tree or plant which has been planted pursuant to a notice" under s 27(1)
-- -- there is no approval route at all; (4) only the immediate-threat exception.
-- "tree" includes a single-stemmed palm and its seedling, sapling or reshoot (s 2). "cut" means felling or lopping (s 2).
-- The officer exemption is encoded only for national parks and nature reserves, where s 8(4) states it.
GIVEN `the place` IS A Place, `girth in metres` IS A NUMBER, `immediate threat to life or property` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Commissioner determined it dying or dead` IS A BOOLEAN, `an officer acting in duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `cutting is restricted without approval` IF
    CONSIDER `the place`
    WHEN `a national park` THEN NOT `an officer acting in duty`
    WHEN `a nature reserve` THEN NOT `an officer acting in duty`
    WHEN `a tree conservation area` THEN `girth in metres` > 1 AND (NOT `immediate threat to life or property`)
    WHEN `vacant land` THEN `girth in metres` > 1 AND (NOT `immediate threat to life or property`)
    WHEN `a heritage road green buffer` THEN (NOT `immediate threat to life or property`) AND (NOT `the Commissioner determined it dying or dead`)
    WHEN `a green margin planted under a s 27 notice` THEN NOT `immediate threat to life or property`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 27(2) has no approval route: approval from the Commissioner cannot make the cutting lawful. ss 8, 14, 18 each allow approval
-- under s 12 or s 20.
GIVEN `the place` IS A Place
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an approval route exists` IF
    CONSIDER `the place`
    WHEN `a national park` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a nature reserve` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a tree conservation area` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `vacant land` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a heritage road green buffer` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the place` IS A Place, `girth in metres` IS A NUMBER, `immediate threat to life or property` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Commissioner determined it dying or dead` IS A BOOLEAN, `an officer acting in duty` IS A BOOLEAN, `has approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `cutting the tree is an offence` IF
        `cutting is restricted without approval` `the place` `girth in metres` `immediate threat to life or property` `the Commissioner determined it dying or dead` `an officer acting in duty`
    AND ((NOT `has approval`) OR (NOT `an approval route exists` `the place`))

§§ `9(3) -- releasing animals`

-- s 9(3): must not, without approval, "(a) bring or release into, or abandon any animal in ... a nature reserve; (b) release or abandon
-- ... into any river, stream, canal or watercourse outside a nature reserve that the person knows, or ought reasonably to know, flows
-- into or through the nature reserve; or (c) permit any animal ... to stray into a nature reserve." The subsection names nature
-- reserves only, not national parks. (s 9(1)(a) separately restricts capturing, displacing or FEEDING any animal within a national park
-- or nature reserve.)
GIVEN `released into a nature reserve` IS A BOOLEAN, `released into a watercourse known to flow into a nature reserve` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `released into a national park` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the release falls under s 9(3)` IF
    `released into a nature reserve` OR `released into a watercourse known to flow into a nature reserve`

§§ `Part 8 and offence sections -- maximum penalties`

-- s 8(3), s 9(4): fine not exceeding $50,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 6 months or both; continuing offence $500 a day.
-- s 10(3): fine not exceeding $20,000.
-- s 14(2): "cut[s] ... or damages any tree" -- fine not exceeding $50,000; (3) court to regard "any financial benefit".
-- s 18(2): $50,000 (same financial-benefit regard, (3)).  s 19(2): $50,000, continuing $500 a day.
-- s 24(2): building works without planting-area approval -- $30,000, continuing $500.  s 26(2): $30,000, continuing $500.
-- s 27(3): $30,000.  s 43: obstructing -- $10,000 or 6 months or both.  s 44(1): parking on a green verge or turfed open space -- $10,000.
-- s 46(1): failing to comply with a notice or condition of approval -- $20,000, continuing "not exceeding $200" a day.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `s 8 harming trees or plants in a national park or nature reserve`
    `s 9 harming animals in a national park or nature reserve`
    `s 10 damaging a notice or boundary mark`
    `s 14 cutting a large tree in a tree conservation area or vacant land`
    `s 18 cutting in a heritage road green buffer`
    `s 19 interfering with a heritage road green buffer`
    `s 24 building works without planting-area approval`
    `s 26 interfering with a planting area`
    `s 27 cutting a tree planted under notice`
    `s 43 obstructing an officer`
    `s 44 parking on a green verge`
    `s 46 not complying with a notice or condition`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 8 harming trees or plants in a national park or nature reserve` THEN 50000
    WHEN `s 9 harming animals in a national park or nature reserve` THEN 50000
    WHEN `s 10 damaging a notice or boundary mark` THEN 20000
    WHEN `s 14 cutting a large tree in a tree conservation area or vacant land` THEN 50000
    WHEN `s 18 cutting in a heritage road green buffer` THEN 50000
    WHEN `s 19 interfering with a heritage road green buffer` THEN 50000
    WHEN `s 24 building works without planting-area approval` THEN 30000
    WHEN `s 26 interfering with a planting area` THEN 30000
    WHEN `s 27 cutting a tree planted under notice` THEN 30000
    WHEN `s 43 obstructing an officer` THEN 10000
    WHEN `s 44 parking on a green verge` THEN 10000
    WHEN `s 46 not complying with a notice or condition` THEN 20000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 8 harming trees or plants in a national park or nature reserve` THEN 6
    WHEN `s 9 harming animals in a national park or nature reserve` THEN 6
    WHEN `s 43 obstructing an officer` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE 0

-- The daily figure for continuing offences after conviction. s 46(1) says "not exceeding $200"; the others say "a further fine of
-- $500" without "not exceeding".
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the continuing daily fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 8 harming trees or plants in a national park or nature reserve` THEN 500
    WHEN `s 9 harming animals in a national park or nature reserve` THEN 500
    WHEN `s 19 interfering with a heritage road green buffer` THEN 500
    WHEN `s 24 building works without planting-area approval` THEN 500
    WHEN `s 26 interfering with a planting area` THEN 500
    WHEN `s 46 not complying with a notice or condition` THEN 200
    OTHERWISE 0

-- ss 14(3), 18(3): "the court is to, in particular, have regard to any financial benefit which has accrued or appears likely to
-- accrue to the person in consequence of the offence."
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court must regard financial benefit` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 14 cutting a large tree in a tree conservation area or vacant land` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 18 cutting in a heritage road green buffer` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `51 -- composition`

-- s 51(1): the Commissioner may compound an offence "prescribed as a compoundable offence" by collecting "a sum not exceeding the
-- lower of": (a) "one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence"; (b) "$5,000". Which offences are
-- prescribed as compoundable is left to regulations, which were not retrieved; the cap below assumes the offence is prescribed.
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS IF `a` < `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the composition cap for a maximum fine` MEANS `the lower of` (`maximum fine` / 2) 5000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the composition cap` MEANS `the composition cap for a maximum fine` (`the maximum fine` `the offence`)

§§ `45 -- the vehicle owner`

-- s 45(1): when an offence is committed "in relation to a vehicle", the owner "shall be guilty of the offence in all respects as if
-- the person were the actual offender ... unless the court is satisfied that the vehicle was at the relevant time a stolen vehicle or
-- a vehicle illegally taken or used". (3): not guilty if the owner "(a) within 14 days after service ... of a notice ... provides by a
-- statement in writing to the Commissioner stating truthfully the name and address of the person who was in charge of the vehicle"
-- or "(b) satisfies the court that the owner did not know and would not with reasonable diligence have ascertained such name and
-- address". (2): once a penalty is imposed on or recovered from one person, none from another.
GIVEN `the vehicle was stolen or illegally taken` IS A BOOLEAN, `days after the notice the driver was named` IS A NUMBER,
      `the driver was named truthfully in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `owner could not have ascertained the driver` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a penalty already imposed on another person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner is liable` IF
        (NOT `the vehicle was stolen or illegally taken`)
    AND (NOT (`the driver was named truthfully in writing` AND `days after the notice the driver was named` <= 14))
    AND (NOT `owner could not have ascertained the driver`)
    AND (NOT `a penalty already imposed on another person`)

§§ `46(2) -- the due-diligence defence`

-- s 46(1): "without reasonable excuse" fails to comply with a notice or contravenes a condition of approval. (2): "it is a defence
-- for that person charged to prove to the satisfaction of the court that that person has used all due diligence to comply".
GIVEN `failed to comply` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved all due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `non-compliance is an offence` IF
    `failed to comply` AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`) AND (NOT `proved all due diligence`)

§§ `56 -- appeal to the Minister`

-- s 56(1): a person aggrieved by a notice listed there, or a refusal of approval under s 12, 20 or 32, "may, within 14 days from the
-- date of service of the notice, or the date the person is notified of the Commissioner's decision, appeal to the Minister".
-- (2): "Despite any appeal ..., the notice or decision appealed against takes effect and must be complied with unless otherwise
-- ordered by the Minister." (5): the Minister's decision is final.
GIVEN `days since service or notification` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal is in time` IF `days since service or notification` <= 14

GIVEN `an appeal is pending` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Minister ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice must still be complied with` IF NOT `the Minister ordered otherwise`

§§ `3 -- the Government and its contractors`

-- s 3(1): the Act binds the Government "except that nothing in this Act renders the Government liable to prosecution for an
-- offence". (2): "no person is immune from prosecution ... by reason that the person is a contractor engaged to provide services to
-- the Government".
DECLARE Defendant IS ONE OF
    `the Government`
    `a Government contractor`
    `a private person`

GIVEN `the defendant` IS A Defendant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `can be prosecuted` IF
    CONSIDER `the defendant`
    WHEN `the Government` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE
